# What `eas build` leaves out of the project it uploads. When this file exists EAS reads it instead
# of every .gitignore, so it repeats what the root and apps/mobile .gitignore files leave out, and
# adds the folders a phone build never needs. Without it the upload was 438 MB, almost all of it
# old session worktrees under .claude/ that only a local git exclude hides, and one iPhone upload
# timed out at 328 MB (Oct 10, 2026). With it the upload is about 9 MB.

# Root .gitignore
node_modules/
test-results/
playwright-report/
_site/
.env
.env.production
.DS_Store
backups/
*.p8
*.p12
*.mobileprovision

# apps/mobile/.gitignore
apps/mobile/.expo/
apps/mobile/dist/
apps/mobile/web-build/
apps/mobile/expo-env.d.ts
apps/mobile/ios/
apps/mobile/android/
.kotlin/
*.orig.*
*.jks
*.key
*.pem
.metro-health-check*
npm-debug.*
yarn-debug.*
yarn-error.*
.env*.local
*.tsbuildinfo

# Never needed by a phone build
.claude/
